   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity 1.1 _ Existence of regional Centers of Excellence for Independent Living
Activity 1.2_ Number of units in selected communities with mental health identification at primary care
Activity 1.3_Nationwide survey conducted, and National AT List updated and submitted for Gov approval
Activity 1.4_Number of regions with personal assistants institutions and family support system
Activity 2.1_Systems of data collection on disability are functional and effectively feed evidence-based policy formulation
Activity 2.2_Existence of a national policy on service provision and assistive technology; Existence of a national Strategy for Early Childhood Development
Activity 2.3_ Survey on children with disabilities;  Research and analytical capacity is built in 3 centers to ensure scientific support to the new policy framework on disability assessment and service provision.
Activity 2.4_Existence of gender-sensitive and age-specific Individual Service Delivery Plans for children/adults 
Activity 3.1_Number of policy makers trained and applying the knowledge in the policy formulation
Activity 3.2_Number of regions with trained health, social and education professionals /service providers; Increased number of families of children with disabilities receive tailored services to reduce likelihood of lifelong sequels
Activity 3.3_The modernized and strengthened service provision centers have sufficient technical and human resources to provide quality services to children and adults with disabilities. 
Activity 3.4_Model curricula for targeted groups of health care, rehabilitation and habilitation service providers developed.
Activity 4.1_Number of regions where persons/children with disabilities are informed about their rights and can exercise them effectively.
Activity 4.2_Number of innovative methods and tools developed and applied.</narrative>
    </description>
